{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction: an earlier Phase 1 RCA comment on this ticket described the separate pytest env-var length failure and belongs to `watertight-sirenian-auk`. The legitimacy checkpoint for THIS ticket is: local runtime simulation with `rebar._store.git_locking.fcntl = None` reproduces `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'` in both `_store_git_op_lock` and `fetch_coordination_lock`, matching CI run 33426859481 (`git_locking.py:224`). But the repository currently states in `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py:19-20` and commit 5697f2e11179 (`rebar-ticket: 0b31-aeb5-e734-41c9`) that actually using fcntl locking off POSIX is out of scope / Windows is not a declared support target; the prior fix deliberately guaranteed collectability only. Per the reporter’s explicit guard, I am not auto-fixing production locking until that support-scope decision is resolved."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788219053209960886,"uuid":"6fc98026-db58-433c-aaa6-5b79744e23ab"}